On Tue, 19 Jun 2007 09:57:45 -0700, Knnn wrote:

> As for keeping track of how  many times a
> scroll has been picked up, according to the spoilers
> I've read this is done through BUC status - that you can
> pick up a scrolls as many times as you want as long as
> you bless it after each use.  If the scrolls are all
> uncursed, you should be able to pick them up from the
> ground exactly the same number of times.

Not quite. You can re-use it as often as you like if you
only ever pick it up while it's blessed, but you can only
pick it up while uncursed once; the second time, it'll
disintegrate. Presumably one of your scrolls has been
picked up while uncursed, and the other two haven't.

For source divers:

        } else  if (obj->otyp == SCR_SCARE_MONSTER) {
            if (obj->blessed) obj->blessed = 0;
            else if (!obj->spe && !obj->cursed) obj->spe = 1;
            else {
                  the scroll disintegrates
            }
        }

The "odd one out" presumably has its "obj->spe" flag set and
won't stack with the others which still have it clear.

